{"n": 14, "utc": "2026-10-31T16:28:31Z", "prev_sha256": "1efb780aea619d320ef0ce47be3cafe27207a5166a62a8d77e5ef0e25f464ca5", "md5": {"data/s/s_1.5.json": "14cd37bf563bc039af48283317096186", "data/s/s_2.json": "76c77fa2f1939badd0cac33f8b640269", "data/ritz_1.5.json": "588a9dd766d02cbff18b000019c49de8", "data/ritz_2.json": "cb983adb43f8bd59d9d91af492880ed7", "out/P0_bench.json": "8b1747c8e10dcc20c2626826a285becb", "grid_run/ref/final_odd_1.5_2o3.json": "8b710199eb4cb5a12d82220ec467704a", "grid_run/ref/final_l2_1.5_1o4.json": "766cad83d1b778b867cbb75696222100", "grid_run/upper/upper640.jsonl": "2878cf86fff2129a640e838aebfac7bc", "grid_run/upper/upper_k384.jsonl": "ea503cee5129f51982bae18212467d54", "grid_run/upper/upper_rerun_L2.jsonl": "948112adea41596fd8e869bc8af1b6d8", "grid_run/upper/upper_1.5_1.jsonl": "97cc19fb7bb2a1b460ae1e3d2fd92ca3"}, "text": "Hand-over to vm3 (GRID_PLAN 6 steps 1-4; grid G VM). From this entry the canonical log is vm3 ~/rh60route/AMENDMENTS.log; the vm4 copy is frozen at entry 13 (md5 370d4a9039aee6d7e6693fe8c8486750, chain sha256 1efb780a...). Approval as stated in the workflow task text: the author approved running grid G on [1.4035, 2] on vm3 (2026-10-31 ~16:50, time zone not stated); vm1/vm2 not touched (Elston grid still running); vm4 read/copy only. Setup: hp/ and upper/ rsynced from vm4 via the laptop (49 files, md5 equal to vm4; the 27 code/ and grid/ files equal to the laptop copies and to the PREREG_GRID.stamp sha256 lines; 49 archive blobs match their sha256 names); code -> hp/lb/rh60route/code. Seeds, sha256 equal to the PREREG_GRID.stamp comments: data/s/s_{1.5,2}.json, data/ritz_{1.5,2}.json, out/P0_bench.json, grid_run/ref/final_{odd_1.5_2o3,l2_1.5_1o4}.json (from vm4); grid_run/upper/upper640.jsonl, upper_k384.jsonl (= laptop gap/out_all/upper.jsonl), upper_rerun_L2.jsonl (laptop pilot/glue); upper_1.5_1.jsonl = line 1 (L 1.5, par 1, K 512) of laptop data/odd.jsonl (sha256 b87cde45... as in the stamp). Environment: ~/weil/.venv Python 3.12.15 (vm4: 3.12.16), python-flint 0.9.0, mpmath 1.4.1, numpy 2.5.4 (no scipy; no grid file imports it); GNU time at /usr/bin/time; glibc 2.43 as on vm4 (sr_kernel copied, not rebuilt; P0 checks it); 64 vCPU, MemTotal 60340 MB, root disk 85 GB free. run_grid.sh unchanged: memory budget 0.85*MemTotal - in use at start (about 49 GB, 15 % headroom), 60 slots. No code change; no grid job has run."}
{"n": 15, "utc": "2026-10-31T23:10:28Z", "prev_sha256": "8fe0ff9b1b35add45089953bb8103b65d030b8e4ce49d1879aa8305ecea5e1d6", "md5": {"hp/lb/rh60route/grid/windows.txt": "1beaea143e1899efac29aa9ff4462ba3", "hp/lb/rh60route/grid/jobs.txt": "12bd6f01a84ff410306ff5c527c52a4d", "grid_run/out/REFINE_1.91455078125_1.92364501953125": "d2890f30b90f8635d46ed156afd194e1"}, "text": "Refinement r1 (PREREG_GRID 2.5, mechanical; this entry is execution step (1), written before windows.txt/jobs.txt change and before any r1 job). Step 43 of 52, [1.91455078125, 1.92364501953125]: job l2_1.92364501953125 exited 4, marker grid_run/out/REFINE_1.91455078125_1.92364501953125 (kind l2): the lambda_2 ladder at 1.92364501953125 ended without a PASS. All 3 rungs (1/4*lam2hat(M0), 2^-10*lam2hat(M0), 2*U^ev(1.91455078125) = 5.15805902827798e-237) FAIL at V4 only (every hard gate true, V5 margin > 0; float p_min -0.643 / -0.133 / -0.132, SR_fail 37375 of 37376 labels at all three; N 37888, M 151552, t_N 0.59-0.62). The odd ladder there passed on 2/3. No STOP_* file; GLUE exited 3 (refinement pending). L prime = 1.91912841796875 = 31443/2^14, the dyadic nearest to 1/2 log((e^{2L_i} + e^{2L_i+1})/2) = 1.91911857640 (= 31442.839/2^14); min |2L prime - log n| over prime powers n = 0.0119 > 2^-20. New windows.txt: L prime inserted after 1.91455078125 (54 windows, 53 steps), md5 74e62f6dc210e167d8147026ce53df5d. jobs.txt gets 10 lines with suffix _r1 (plan.py rules at L prime: K 768, prec 6000, 4.2 GB): U0/U1, S, R, G0 at L prime; grid.py ladder odd|l2 1.91912841796875 1.91455078125; grid.py ladder odd|l2 1.92364501953125 1.91912841796875; GLUE_r1 after all of them. Then REFINE_1.91455078125_1.92364501953125 is renamed REFINED_. Refinements: 1 of 6 (K9g). Operator note before any r1 result: under the reuse rule of 2.5 the rerun lambda_2 ladder at 1.92364501953125 already holds its 3 FAIL records (l2_1.92364501953125_{1o4,1o1024,2}; the V4 failure does not depend on mu), so the refined sub-step [1.91912841796875, 1.92364501953125] is expected to end without a PASS; if so, K3g applies (one refinement level per step)."}
{"n": 16, "utc": "2026-11-01T00:03:59Z", "prev_sha256": "7fa66c0067fb934640df39369489d85336e44388b297f7236e3a94cdae112dd7", "md5": {"grid_run/out/REFINE_1.91912841796875_1.92364501953125": "5cd0c96202be4cda9d71c9d87807c729", "grid_run/logs/GLUE_r1.log": "6b8f2eff3f83c66b7730f7f9e1351d98", "hp/lb/rh60route/grid/jobs.txt": "f77b5459e74bad0af546a0a1523fd776", "hp/lb/rh60route/grid/windows.txt": "74e62f6dc210e167d8147026ce53df5d"}, "text": "Refinement r1 outcome (operator record, no change to any file or rule). Runner restarted 2026-10-31T23:11:30Z on the appended jobs, finished 2026-11-01T00:03:43Z, no STOP_* file. At L prime = 1.91912841796875: U0/U1 exit 0 (K 768, prec 6000; U^ev 2.74710710889347e-239, U^od 3.63609239109277e-234, radius rule rel 9.8e-14 / 9.9e-14, holds; peak 3.57/3.54 GB, wall 2064/2058 s), S, R, G0 exit 0; odd ladder PASS on 2/3 (p_min 0.616), lambda_2 ladder PASS on 1/4 (p_min 0.727). At 1.92364501953125 with L_prev = L prime: odd ladder reused odd_1.92364501953125_2o3 (PASS); lambda_2 ladder reused its 3 FAIL records (cap reached, no new run), exit 4, marker out/REFINE_1.91912841796875_1.92364501953125. GLUE_r1 exit 3: refinement pending, not glued: REFINE_1.91912841796875_1.92364501953125. The refined sub-step [1.91912841796875, 1.92364501953125] has no PASS and PREREG_GRID 2.5 allows one refinement level per step, so no further refinement is made (1 of 6 used); K3g applies: grid G is not viable as registered. The REFINE_ marker is left in place."}
{"n": 17, "utc": "2026-11-01T00:04:26Z", "prev_sha256": "fb6713c00e536d9b230839017fe1dbc1f9b93a1ba1db30567843da21b95478a6", "md5": {}, "text": "Erratum to entries 15-16 (wording only): 5.15805902827798e-237 is U^ev(1.91455078125) itself; the lambda_2 rung-3 record l2_1.92364501953125_2 ran at mu = 2*U^ev(1.91455078125) = 1.0316e-236 and was reused unchanged by l2_1.92364501953125_r1 (its printed hist shows the new reference 2.74710710889347e-239 = U^ev(1.91912841796875), but no run was made at 2*that value)."}
{"n": 18, "utc": "2026-11-01T00:40:41Z", "prev_sha256": "166e782133352ad00a8239a8ff94c7852940dac57d1e015271ba99d674154fcd", "md5": {"diag_gap/certify_diag.py": "223e1b58c34095a6e221130722a67afa", "diag_gap/mkdiag.py": "619cc184e76c4453b88bcad15789e5f4", "diag_gap/edge.py": "fbc61af7ab37e24d9a16f1be26306a44", "hp/lb/rh60route/code/certify.py": "5c14918be1ab9d6c4f5726f794533bb5"}, "text": "POST-HOC DIAGNOSTIC GAP_DIAG (declared before running; never scored; nothing is written to grid_run/, glue/ or data/; no new PREREG is implied). Purpose: diagnose the V4 last-label failures (SR_fail = n-1) at 1.92364501953125 (3 lambda_2 rungs) and 1.8958740234375 (1/4 rung). Code: diag_gap/certify_diag.py = code/certify.py (md5 5c14918b) plus DIAG-only patches built by diag_gap/mkdiag.py: DIAG_N0 (start of the R4 N rule), DIAG_MFAC, an edge profile of S_M near the I_P/F cut, and G5 extended to the labels N-1..N-3. Env: no RH60_STAMP, no RH60_AMEND, RH60_ARCHIVE=diag_gap/archive. Runs on vm3 only, 2 single-core jobs (<= 6 GB): D1 = L 1.92364501953125, mu-rel 1/4 lam2hat, registered N (expect 37888), --sr --save-input (reproduction); D2 = same with DIAG_N0 = 38912 (N + 1024), --sr --save-input (candidate fix). Then float-only diag_gap/edge.py on the saved inputs."}
{"n": 19, "utc": "2026-11-01T01:01:19Z", "prev_sha256": "5e25da345ab51c9156fca5f617833330413ffd510d81fd10c9d12da22e056722", "md5": {"diag_gap/out/diag_D1_N37888.json": "c897857805e3cedc8b372d4a38a9d5dd", "diag_gap/out/diag_D2_N38912.json": "1ea7e9cae541ac854fcdca6052441f83", "diag_gap/out/diag_D1_N37888.input.json": "1fcb9c2240fe2419bb000cb498baf2b9", "diag_gap/out/diag_D2_N38912.input.json": "5d0bd261901faa58957de667b876f8b0", "diag_gap/out/diag_D1_N37888.input.json.edge.json": "0feacbf34dd045209cab678bd440165e", "diag_gap/out/diag_D2_N38912.input.json.edge.json": "375b522d53d427793963a8523d47a7f9", "diag_gap/run.sh": "b196180bcee75cb480a1f09ec12bfee0"}, "text": "POST-HOC DIAGNOSTIC GAP_DIAG outcome (never scored; no file under grid_run/, glue/ or data/ was written; nothing here is a claim). D1 (N 37888, mu 1/4 lam2hat): FAIL at V4 only, SR_fail 37375, float p_min -0.6434, SR_checksum T 122d6632... identical to grid record l2_1.92364501953125_1o4 (bit-exact reproduction); G5 extended to labels N-1..N-3 (3 diagonal, 3 off-diagonal entries) agrees with the direct far sum. Edge profile: interior S_M diagonal median 8.2 with far loss <= 0.002, but at the last label q = 37887 the far loss is 6.31 of S_qq 7.94, 5.25 of it from the single coupling S(37887, 37888) = 1.761 divided by t_N = 0.591; float edge.py: S_input is indefinite even at delta = 0 (last pivot -0.44, one negative eigenvalue, 78 percent of its weight on the last row), so no mu, delta_0 or M = 8N change can pass at N 37888. D2 (N 38912 = N + 1024, else identical): PASS, all 15 gates true, float p_min = SR min pivot 0.8663 (row 38, interior), V5 margin 0.00443, eps_E 9.9e-17, SR_checksum T 13c7013111f097ad..., lower bound 4.5717e-232; edge coupling 0.981, loss 1.75, last diagonal 8.82. Reading: a cut-position (N) boundary effect of the lossy far bound T = diag(t_q) at the I_P/F cut; not a property of lambda_2, not a bug. See GAP_DIAG.md. A fix needs a new PREREG before any scored run."}
